  "title": "Glehni Park & Chamber Tea",
  "date": "2026-11-21T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Glehni Park & Chamber Tea\n\nAttended Larsen's hiking club. Today, we went to Glehni Park.\n\nRight now, most of the park is owned by TalTech, including the castle and the tower.\n\nCastle\n\nGlehn built this park and the sculpture of the Estonian giant hero Kalevipoeg fighting a dragon. Yes, the crocodile in the picture is supposed to be a dragon, but Estonians don't buy it. They call the sculpture Glehn's Devil.\n\nGlehni Kurat\n\nThe dragon\n\nThe tower\n\nAfter the hiking, I went to JYSK to buy a humidifier. It was the last one in the shop and cost me 14.5 EUR.\n\nhumidifier\n\nThen I went to Chamber tea shop to attend a meetup organized by The Kind Circle MTÜ. I hadn't spoken Chinese in a long time.\n\nChamber tea\n\ntea hour\n\nselfie",
